  "chapter": 320,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 14  Chapter 320\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7227, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public officers law, in relation to the dates\n        by which  the  governor  may  make  proclamation  of  a  special\n        election to fill certain offices\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  requires  that the Governor issue a proclamation to call a\nspecial election within 10 days of a vacancy in an elective office,  and\nshortens  the  time  frame  for  holding  such  special election for all\noffices, except for representatives in Congress, to not less than  forty\ndays  nor more than fifty days from the date of the proclamation to fill\nthe vacancy. Finally, when there is a vacancy on or after April 1 of the\nlast year of the term of office, this bill sets a deadline after which a\nspecial election will not be held.\n \n  I have agreed with the legislature to make  a  series  of  changes  to\nensure  that  this  legislation  is  flexible and does not unnecessarily\nburden boards of elections, while also ensuring voters  are  represented\nagain as soon as possible. First, the agreement makes a series of neces-\nsary  technical  and  conforming changes to ensure the election calendar\ncan accommodate the expedited special election cycle. Second, the agree-\nment ensures greater flexibility in which elections are subject  to  the\nexpedited schedule by making the expedited provisions applicable only to\nNew York State Senate and Assembly races. Finally, the agreement permits\nthe  Governor  to  schedule multiple vacancies that occur within 30 days\nbefore a previously scheduled special election for the  same  day.  This\nwill   ensure   better  efficiency  in  the  administration  of  special\nelections.\n\n  With these agreed upon changes, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  The bill is approved.                       (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
